         decode (`bool`, defaults to `True`):
             Whether to decode the image data. If `False`,
             returns the underlying dictionary in the format `{"path": image_path, "bytes": image_bytes}`.
+        crop_margin (`int`, *optional*):
+            Number of pixels to crop from each of the four edges of the image when it is decoded, for example
+            to remove a watermark or a border. If `None` or `0`, the image is not cropped. It must not be
+            negative, and the image must be larger than twice the margin in both dimensions.
